<title>USA: USX-Marathon unit income rises.</title>
<headline>USX-Marathon unit income rises.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>USX-Marathon Group said Thursday that worldwide exploration and production operating income was $251 million in the fourth quarter, compared to $105 million the previous fourth quarter.</p>
<p>Domestic upstream income was $137 million in the fourth quarter, versus $66 million the year before.</p>
<p>Domestic gas production in 1996 rose 42 million cubic feet per day compared to 676.0 million cubic feet in 1995.</p>
<p>International upstream operating income was $114 million in the fourth quarter versus $39 million.</p>
<p>Refining, marketing and transportation posted earnings of $73 million, versus $19 million for the fourth quarter.</p>
</text>
